{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/14ryd8fq","slide":3,"text":"A rally ending by day 10 can influence every cumulative forward cell whose horizon is at least 10 sessions.","textPreview":"A rally ending by day 10 can influence every cumulative forward cell whose horizon is at least 10 sessions.","textChars":107,"textLines":1,"bbox":[350,576,820,52]}
{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/ofy9wn61","slide":3,"text":"Cumulative future returns are nested: R(1:100) = R(1:10) + R(11:100). If the signal is related only to R(1:10), that covariance is still carried inside R(1:20), R(1:50), and R(1:100). Later independent noise may attenuate the correlation, but it does not mechanically erase the early contribution. This is why an early 5–10-session rebound can remain visible at 100.\n\n[Sources]\n- Codex thread 01a0226e-2fa2-7222-a6d9-79ab971ac616 (2026-08-27), operator–Codex huddle immediately following the full-vocabulary atlas closeout.\n- operator_hypothesis_lab/presentations/tsla_descriptive_microscope_evidence.pptx, especially slides 105 and 114–123.\n[/Sources]"}
