{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/x8f69ofe","slide":6,"text":"A daily signal with a 100-session holding period can generate many overlapping positions and near-continuous market exposure. Compare it with unconditional drift, the same regime without the prior-loss condition, and matched long exposure. Data-snooping controls become relevant once variants are compared or performance is ranked.\n\n[Sources]\n- Codex thread 01a0226e-2fa2-7222-a6d9-79ab971ac616 (2026-08-27), operator–Codex huddle immediately following the full-vocabulary atlas closeout.\n- Halbert White (2000), A Reality Check for Data Snooping, https://doi.org/10.1111/1468-0262.00152\n- Bailey et al., The Probability of Backtest Overfitting, https://www.davidhbailey.com/dhbpapers/backtest-prob.pdf\n- Bailey and López de Prado, The Deflated Sharpe Ratio, https://papers.ssrn.com/sol3/papers.cfm?abstract_id=2460551\n[/Sources]"}
